            <ArticleTitle>Acute urinary retention due to ectopic pregnancy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>44-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two cases of ectopic pregnancy are presented in which acute urinary retention was a salient clinical feature. The emergency physician must consider ectopic pregnancy in the differential diagnosis in any woman of child-bearing age with abdominal, pelvic, or urinary complaints.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
